# #5837. Under the claimless advance an activation learns its bounds only from the
# responses to its own appends, which carry both the foreignHigh and the shared
# unstamped watermark, so either restart floor alone covers the offsets a WAL shard
# restart forgot (ReadPositionHonestPreArmWatermarkNotReset is clean under
# WithFreeAdvance). Without both, a duplicate's append before the restart is passed.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestFreeAdvanceRestartForgetsBothFloors
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a WAL shard restart keeps neither the foreignHigh start-head floor nor the shared watermark's reset
PERTURBS: Restart
BOUNDS: WithFreeAdvance = TRUE, WithRestart = TRUE, WithEvict = FALSE, MaxWindows = 0

--- FIND
    Max({startHead - 1, evFloor} \cup {o \in Offs : o >= TrackStart /\ author[o] \in Acts \ {a}}
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: no shardStartHead - 1 fallback.
    Max({-1, evFloor} \cup {o \in Offs : o >= TrackStart /\ author[o] \in Acts \ {a}}
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ restarted' = TRUE
    /\ lastU' = next - 1
--- REPLACE
    /\ restarted' = TRUE
\* MUTATION: the shared watermark is lost with the shard's memory.
    /\ lastU' = -1
--- END
